! mcp_bootstrap_p148.strap -- the console-message tail of the Z EC75
! error routine, the MCP write-control-word block, and the entry
! point S DSPDS, printed page 148.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF
! p.155, banner read and not assumed: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11011MCP   CARD ID HA000047   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER
! 148".
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS.  Thirty printed lines, no asterisk box, no SLC.
! Lines 1-8 finish a routine that came in from printed p.147: it
! loads the message address, SICs into J ZECM, branches to J ZECBR,
! restores the IODEF branch, picks up Z EC75S, bumps the MCP control
! word's count field and leaves for Z EC99.  Lines 9-19 are the
! DATA the routine uses -- two control words, a two-word
! reservation, four DDs of bit patterns, an eight-bit IQS message,
! a one-word reservation and two VF cells.  Line 20 is a bare
! comment card, "***** ENTER HERE FROM B, DMCP ERROR ******", and
! lines 21-30 are S DSPDS, the error-display entry: it waits on an
! indicator, sets $14, saves the IC, restores two groups of index
! registers through S T LR, returns through a masked BE, waits
! again, loads the error code S BR40, SICs into S DISIC and leaves
! for S DISP.
!
! TWENTY-FIVE CARDS OVER THIRTY LINES.  The serial column runs
! HA000047 (line 1) to HA000071 (line 30), and five serials are
! printed on two lines each -- HA000048 on lines 2 AND 3, HA000067
! on 22 and 23, HA000068 on 24 and 25, HA000069 on 26 and 27, and
! HA000071 on 29 and 30.  Each of those is one card carrying two
! statements; the SIC/branch pairs (2,3) and (29,30) are the
! familiar case and (22,23), (24,25), (26,27) are three more.
! 30 - 5 = 25 cards.  NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END: the banner's own
! CARD ID is HA000047, which is line 1's serial, and the paper
! below line 30 is blank to the foot of the form.
!
! >>> THE SURVEY UNDER-READ THIS PAGE BY NINE ROWS. <<<  It reported
! 21 rows, 217433.40..217457.4, and classed the page MIXED on one
! trailing "+".  The page has THIRTY rows, 217432.40..217457.40, it
! lost line 1 off the top (which is what the brief warned about),
! and there are FOUR "+" rows, not one -- lines 9, 10, 18 and 19.
! Counted off the card-serial column, not off the survey.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NEAR SIDE.  This page prints NO "SLC", so the deck writes a hard
! "SLC,(8)217432.40", which ASSERTS the origin rather than checking
! it (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE
! WITH THE ARRIVING COUNTER").  Two independent witnesses pay that
! back:
!
!   * THE HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS NOT BLANK ON THIS
!     PAGE.  It prints "LOCATION   217432" -- IBM's assembler
!     stating the origin WORD.  It carries no bit offset, so it
!     cannot settle .00 against .40; the ".40" is read off line 1's
!     LOCATION column alone.
!   * printed p.147's last line is at 217432.00 and is a half word
!     ("217451.03 30   Z EC75   LV,1,ZEC75S"), so the counter leaves
!     p.147 at exactly 217432.40.  Read out of
!     docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt, which is an OCR of ANOTHER
!     printed page and therefore a legitimate index -- the volume
!     OCR of p.148 itself would not be a witness for p.148.
!
! FAR SIDE, PREDICTED AND THEN CONFIRMED.  Line 30 is a half-word
! branch whose printed LOCATION is 217457.40, so the counter leaves
! this page at 217460.00 and printed p.149's first row must be
! 217460.00.  CHECKED BEFORE LANDING, against the volume OCR of
! PDF p.156 (printed p.149) -- another page, so a legitimate index:
! after its four-line asterisk box ("THE ERROR DUMP ROUTINE") its
! first emitting row is "A ELM PT  DD(BU,45),..." at 217460.00, and
! the next row it prints is 217460.55.  The join closes.
!
! AND NO SIC/BRANCH PAIR STRADDLES THIS BREAK.  Lines 29 and 30 are
! "SIC,SDISIC" and "B,SDISP" and they share ONE card, HA000071, so
! the pair closes inside the page -- the hazard printed pp.131/132
! ran into does not arise here, and p.149's transcriber inherits no
! orphaned SIC.  p.149's own first statement is a DD, not a branch.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE HEADLINE: THIS IS THE DEFINING PAGE FOR S DISIC. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Eleven landed decks name SDISIC and SEVEN of them SYN it at
! (8)217451.40 -- pp.103, 119, 120, 124, 129, 130 and 143, counted
! with "grep -l '^SDISIC' decks/*.strap" and not off the citation
! comments -- every one of those values BACK-DERIVED from a printed
! "SIC,SDISIC" operand
! half word or, on p.103 line 43, from "BD,SDISIC+.32".  None of
! them had seen its defining card.  Line 19 of THIS page is that
! card:
!
!     19*  217451.40   000000.00+      S DISIC   VF,0
!
! and this deck's counter, started at 217432.40 and carried through
! two control words, a DRZ(N),(2), four DDs, a 112-bit IQS message
! and a DRZ(N),(1), arrives at 217451.40 on its own.  The agreement
! is digit for digit and it is not a tautology: nothing in this deck
! was set to make it come out.  It also confirms p.103's
! "SDISIC+.32 -> 217452.04" arithmetic, because SDISIC+.32 is
! 217452.00, which is line 21's printed LOCATION for S DSPDS.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED, AND HOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) DR vs DRZ, THE ONE THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE.  Lines 11 and 17
!     reserve 2 and 1 words.  A reservation prints its COUNT, so
!     "DR" and "DRZ" compile to the same printed row and the
!     difference is three words of zero CONTENT in the merged image.
!     Rendered at 1800 dpi, both rows print "DRZ(N),(2)" and
!     "DRZ(N),(1)" with the Z unmistakable -- a tall Z with its full
!     diagonal, nothing like the (N) beside it.  Read off the ink,
!     not off a passing run.  (This is the error decks/
!     mcp_bootstrap_p136.strap made in the other direction.)
! (2) S DSPDS (line 21) IS THE ONE NAME ON THIS PAGE THAT RESTS ON
!     INK ALONE.  No other page in the listing names it -- p.103
!     reaches the same address as "SDISIC+.32", by arithmetic, not
!     by name -- so no merge and no !CHECK could ever catch a
!     misspelling.  Six glyphs, two of them the D that this drum
!     prints with the bowl worn through.  Rendered at 1800 dpi
!     beside line 19's "S DISIC": both D's in S D S P D S show the
!     straight vertical LEFT STEM and squared corners, against the
!     stemless round C that ends S DISIC two rows above, in the same
!     column off the same drum.
! (3) THE BIT PATTERN ON LINE 26 IS "111101", NOT "1111C1".  At
!     400 dpi the fifth glyph reads as an open C.  It cannot be one
!     -- the field is a bit pattern -- and the ASSEMBLER SETTLES IT
!     OUTRIGHT, because every bit of it is visible in the printed
!     half word.  Measured, varying nothing else:
!         BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101  ->  215231.47 A0   (printed)
!         BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111111  ->  215231.47 E0
!         BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111100  ->  215231.47 80
!         BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)011101  ->  215231.43 A0
!         BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111001  ->  215231.47 20
!         BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)000000  ->  215231.40 00
!         BE,STLR+1.32   (no mask)   ->  215231.40 00
!     So the printed "215231.47 A0" forces the mask, the ".26" and
!     the "2" together, and line 26 is one of the strongest rows on
!     the page.  The last line of that table also answers the one
!     thing that looked wrong at first reading: printed p.144's
!     "W FINI BE,$" prints "217337.40 00" with byte 00, and a bare
!     BE here prints the same shape.  The .07 and the A0 are
!     entirely the mask operand, not a different operation.
! (4) BLANKS INSIDE NAMES ARE NOT SIGNIFICANT, AND THIS PAGE PROVES
!     IT TWICE IN ITS OWN INK.  Line 18's NAME field prints
!     "Z EC75S" with a clear blank; line 6's STATEMENT references
!     the same symbol as "ZEC75S" with none.  Line 19's name is
!     "S DISIC" and line 29's operand is "SDISIC".  Line 10's name
!     prints closed up as "MMCPCW" while line 7's operand prints
!     "M MCP CW+.43" with two blanks.  The deck writes every one of
!     them closed up, as the deck format requires.
! (5) The IQS datum on line 16 is "TYPE XX ERROR " -- thirteen
!     characters and ONE trailing blank, no blank after the comma.
!     Settled two ways.  By ARITHMETIC: 217446.20 to 217450.00 is
!     112 bits and a converted DD with no byte size is eight bits a
!     character (C28-6129 printed p.16, byte size modulo 8), so the
!     datum is exactly fourteen characters.  By MEASUREMENT: the
!     row was rendered at 1800 dpi and the ink runs fitted to a
!     constant pitch of 180.74 px from the leading "(" to the
!     terminating "*" twenty-seven character positions later; every
!     glyph lands within 10 px of its slot and slots 17, 20 and 26
!     are empty -- one blank between TYPE and XX, one between XX and
!     ERROR, one between ERROR and the "*".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE EIGHT EXTERNALS, AND WHAT EACH ONE RESTS ON
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! J ZECM   217370.00  line 2 prints "217370.00 80" for "SIC,JZECM"
!                     and line 5 prints "217370.35 D0" for
!                     "SVA,14,JZECM" -- two different operations
!                     agreeing on the word.  Corroborated off
!                     ANOTHER printed page: the volume OCR puts a
!                     card at 217370.00 whose name field carries
!                     ZECM, on the page before this one.
!                     >>> ITS BIT OFFSET WITHIN THE HALF WORD IS
!                     UNOBSERVABLE (docs/transcription_workflow.md,
!                     "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" (1)); ".0" is a
!                     convention, not a reading.  The HALF word IS
!                     checked.
! J ZECBR  217362.40  line 3 prints "217362.50 00" for "B,JZECBR"
!                     and a plain B prints target + .10.  The volume
!                     OCR of the PREVIOUS printed page carries the
!                     defining card, "14* 217362.40 ... JZECBR
!                     SIC,K CONVR", which is an independent witness
!                     for the .40 half word.  Bit offset
!                     unobservable.
! K SUPP   216242.00  already landed: decks/mcp_bootstrap_p123.strap
!                     SYNs it at (8)216242.0 off printed p.123 line
!                     2's own defining card, "K SUPP NOP,K COMM".
!                     Line 4 here prints "216242.35 01".
! Z EC99   217421.40  line 8 prints "217421.50 00" for "B,Z EC99".
!                     The volume OCR of the previous printed page
!                     prints its defining card at 217421.40,
!                     "Z EC99 LV,14,SYCOCH -CONSOLE CHANNEL NUMBER".
!                     Bit offset within the half word unobservable.
! S TIC    215265.00  landed by pp.103/119/144 and others; line 23
!                     prints "215265.35 D0".
! S T LR   215230.00  landed by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p144.strap off
!                     printed p.116.  THIS PAGE CHECKS THE
!                     ARITHMETIC THREE TIMES OFF ONE BASE: line 24's
!                     bare S TLR prints 215230, line 25's STLR+14.0
!                     prints 215246 (fourteen DECIMAL words on) and
!                     line 26's STLR+1.32 prints 215231.40 under the
!                     mask.  Three different offsets, one symbol.
! S BR40   000406.00  landed by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p107.strap,
!                     which carries its DEFINING card -- "SBR40
!                     SYN,(16)0106.0", printed p.107 line 21,
!                     000406.00+.  An INTEGER, not an address: line
!                     28's "LVI,$14,SBR40" loads it as the error
!                     code.  Written here in p.107's own hex form so
!                     the two decks cannot drift.
! S DISP   217372.00  landed by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p119.strap off
!                     its lines 43/46, which print 217372.10 for
!                     "B,SDISP" exactly as line 30 here does.  Bit
!                     offset within the half word unobservable.
!
! >>> NO MERGE HAZARD, CHECKED ACROSS EVERY DECK AND NOT JUST THE
! p.1xx ONES. <<<  MCCW1, MMCPCW, MCPBAD, ZEC75M, ZEC75S and SDSPDS
! appear in NO landed deck under any spelling.  SDISIC appears in
! eleven and is SYNned in six, every one at (8)217451.40, which is
! where this page defines it.  Nothing to reconcile.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   1*  217432.40     217450.03 01                                        LVI,1,Z EC75M                   -GET MESSAGE ADDRESS            HA000047
!   2*  217433.00     217370.00 80                                        SIC,JZECM                                                       HA000048
!   3*  217433.40     217362.50 00                                        B,JZECBR                                                        HA000048
!   4*  217434.00 *   216242.35 01                                        LVI,14,KSUPP                                                    HA000049
!   5*  217434.40     217370.35 D0                                        SVA,14,JZECM                    -RESTORE IODEF BRANCH           HA000050
!   6*  217435.00     217451.02 30                                        LV,1,ZEC75S                                                     HA000051
!   7*  217435.40     217440.53 80  003000.22 B0                          M+1(BU,3),M MCP CW+.43          -UPDATE CONTROL WORD            HA000052
!   8*  217436.40     217421.50 00                                        B,Z EC99                                                        HA000053
!   9*  217437.00     000000.00+ 000 000000 000000       MCCW1            CW,0                            -COPIED CW                      HA000054
!  10*  217440.00     217443.00+ 000 000005 000000       MMCPCW           CW,MCPBAD,5.0                   -WRITE CW                       HA000055
!  11*  217441.00 *   000002.00                                           DRZ(N),(2)                                                      HA000056
!  12*  217443.00     1777777777777777777777             MCPBAD           DD(BU),(16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF     -11111......                    HA000057
!  13*  217444.00     1252525252525252525252                              DD(BU),(16)AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA     -........                       HA000058
!  14*  217445.00     1777777777740000000000                              DD(BU),(16)FFFFFFFF00000000     -111111......                   HA000059
!  15*  217446.00     176775                                              DD(BU,16),(16)FDFD              -TWO CARRIAGE RETURNS           HA000060
!  16*  217446.20                                                         (IQS*)DD(BU),TYPE XX ERROR *                                    HA000061
!  17*  217450.00 *   000001.00                          Z EC75M          DRZ(N),(1)                                                      HA000062
!  18*  217451.00     000000.00+                         Z EC75S          VF,0.0                                                          HA000063
!  19*  217451.40     000000.00+                       \ S DISIC          VF,0                            -LOCATION GENERATING ERROR CODE HA000064
!  20*                                                    -               ***** ENTER HERE FROM B, DMCP ERROR ******                      HA000065
!  21*  217452.00     217452.52 C6                        SDSPDS          BIFZ,$.32                                                       HA000066
!  22*  217452.40     000040.35 01                                        LVI,$14,32.0                                                    HA000067
!  23*  217453.00     215265.35 D0                                        SVA,$14,STIC                                                    HA000067
!  24*  217453.40     000003.00 80  215230.34 A0                          TI,14,3.0,STLR                                                  HA000068
!  25*  217454.40     000021.00 80  215246.36 A0                          TI,15,17.0,STLR+14.0                                            HA000068
!  26*  217455.40     215231.47 A0                                        BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101                                       HA000069
!  27*  217456.00     217456.47 C6                                        BOPZ,$.32                                                       HA000069
!  28*  217456.40     000406.35 01                                        LVI,$14,SBR40                                                   HA000070
!  29*  217457.00     217451.40 80                                        SIC,SDISIC                                                      HA000071
!  30*  217457.40     217372.10 00                                        B,SDISP                                                         HA000071
!
! The "*" printed after the LOCATION on lines 4, 11 and 17 is the
! same unexplained second asterisk decks/mcp_bootstrap_p144.strap
! records on its line 21 and p.137 on its lines 20 and 26.  It is
! not read as part of any field.
!
! The "\" printed to the LEFT of the NAME column on line 19 is a
! short diagonal tick in the margin, a character-width and a half
! clear of where "Z" and "S" start on lines 17, 18 and 19.  It is a
! mark on the paper, not a character of the name: "S DISIC" is six
! letters and a blank, and the deck's counter lands it at 217451.40
! without it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS CHECKED AND WHAT IS NOT -- 26 OF 30 ROWS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Four rows carry no !CHECK, and each exclusion is bounded:
!   line 11, line 17  DRZ.  The BINARY OUTPUT column prints the
!       RESERVATION COUNT (000002.00, 000001.00), not storage, so
!       there is nothing for the oracle to compare; pp.84, 109, 114,
!       119, 120, 129 and 139 give their DRZ rows no !CHECK for
!       exactly this reason.  NOTHING ABOUT THEM IS UNKNOWN: line
!       11's two words are pinned by MCPBAD landing on its printed
!       217443.00 (!SYM), and line 17's one word by ZEC75S landing
!       on its printed 217451.00.  A wrong count would move both.
!   line 16  the entry-mode DD prints NOTHING in the BINARY OUTPUT
!       column.  Its 112 bits are pinned from both ends -- it starts
!       at the printed 217446.20 (which line 15's 16-bit DD fixes)
!       and Z EC75M lands on its printed 217450.00 (!SYM) -- and the
!       pitch measurement in GLYPHS (5) fixes which 14 characters.
!   line 20  a bare comment card.  It emits nothing and has no
!       LOCATION.
! The other twenty-six all carry a !CHECK, and seven names carry a
! !SYM against the page's own LOCATION column.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATION HIT: NONE.
! Every statement was handed to strap_asm exactly as printed and
! every one was accepted on the first pass -- including "CW,0" and
! "CW,MCPBAD,5.0", "DRZ(N),(2)", "(IQS*)DD(BU),TYPE XX ERROR *",
! the bare "VF,0", "M+1(BU,3),M MCP CW+.43" and the masked
! "BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101".  No substitution anywhere.  The only
! transformations are the two the deck format requires: blanks
! squeezed out of names (GLYPHS (4)) and the hard SLC for an origin
! the page does not print (THE JOIN).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ---- externals -------------------------------------------------
JZECM   SYN, (8)217370.0             ! p.147's own card; bit offset unobservable
JZECBR  SYN, (8)217362.40            ! p.147's own card "JZECBR SIC,K CONVR"
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! landed by p.123 off p.123 line 2
ZEC99   SYN, (8)217421.40            ! p.147's "Z EC99 LV,14,SYCOCH"
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0             ! landed by pp.103/119/144
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0             ! landed by p.144 off printed p.116
SBR40   SYN, (16)0106.0              ! p.107 line 21's DEFINING card, 000406.00+
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! landed by p.119 off its lines 43/46

! ---- the origin ------------------------------------------------
! The page prints no SLC.  Heading row: "LOCATION   217432"; line
! 1's LOCATION column supplies the ".40".
        SLC, (8)217432.40

! ---- the page --------------------------------------------------
        LVI,1,ZEC75M                        ! line  1  -GET MESSAGE ADDRESS
        SIC,JZECM                           ! line  2
        B,JZECBR                            ! line  3  (same card as 2)
        LVI,14,KSUPP                        ! line  4
        SVA,14,JZECM                        ! line  5  -RESTORE IODEF BRANCH
        LV,1,ZEC75S                         ! line  6
        M+1(BU,3),MMCPCW+.43                ! line  7  -UPDATE CONTROL WORD
        B,ZEC99                             ! line  8
MCCW1   CW,0                                ! line  9  -COPIED CW
MMCPCW  CW,MCPBAD,5.0                       ! line 10  -WRITE CW
        DRZ(N),(2)                          ! line 11
MCPBAD  DD(BU),(16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF         ! line 12  -11111......
        DD(BU),(16)AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA         ! line 13  -........
        DD(BU),(16)FFFFFFFF00000000         ! line 14  -111111......
        DD(BU,16),(16)FDFD                  ! line 15  -TWO CARRIAGE RETURNS
        (IQS*)DD(BU),TYPE XX ERROR *        ! line 16
ZEC75M  DRZ(N),(1)                          ! line 17
ZEC75S  VF,0.0                              ! line 18
SDISIC  VF,0                                ! line 19  -LOCATION GENERATING ERROR CODE
!                                           ! line 20  ***** ENTER HERE FROM B, DMCP ERROR ******
SDSPDS  BIFZ,$.32                           ! line 21
        LVI,$14,32.0                        ! line 22
        SVA,$14,STIC                        ! line 23  (same card as 22)
        TI,14,3.0,STLR                      ! line 24
        TI,15,17.0,STLR+14.0                ! line 25  (same card as 24)
        BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101           ! line 26
        BOPZ,$.32                           ! line 27  (same card as 26)
        LVI,$14,SBR40                       ! line 28
        SIC,SDISIC                          ! line 29
        B,SDISP                             ! line 30  (same card as 29)

!SYM   MCCW1    217437.00
!SYM   MMCPCW   217440.00
!SYM   MCPBAD   217443.00
!SYM   ZEC75M   217450.00
!SYM   ZEC75S   217451.00
!SYM   SDISIC   217451.40
!SYM   SDSPDS   217452.00
!CHECK 217432.40 | 217450.03 01 | line 1 LVI,1,ZEC75M -GET MESSAGE ADDRESS -- the .03 is LVI's own operation bits (index 1); ZEC75M is line 17 on this page
!CHECK 217433.00 | 217370.00 80 | line 2 SIC,JZECM
!CHECK 217433.40 | 217362.50 00 | line 3 B,JZECBR (same card as line 2) -- .50 is JZECBR's .40 plus B's .10
!CHECK 217434.00 | 216242.35 01 | line 4 LVI,14,KSUPP -- index 14 prints .35 (2*14+1 = 0o35), K SUPP landed by p.123
!CHECK 217434.40 | 217370.35 D0 | line 5 SVA,14,JZECM -RESTORE IODEF BRANCH -- same word as line 2, different operation
!CHECK 217435.00 | 217451.02 30 | line 6 LV,1,ZEC75S -- the .02 is LV's index-1 bits; ZEC75S is line 18
!CHECK 217435.40 | 217440.53 80 003000.22 B0 | line 7 M+1(BU,3),MMCPCW+.43 -UPDATE CONTROL WORD -- .43 written DECIMAL and printed 0o53; MMCPCW is line 10, so this row checks the deck's counting from line 7 to line 10
!CHECK 217436.40 | 217421.50 00 | line 8 B,ZEC99
!CHECK 217437.00 | 000000.00+ 000 000000 000000 | line 9 MCCW1 CW,0 -COPIED CW -- printed p.147 line 43 references MCCW1 as 217437.21 and line 44 as MCCW1+.24 -> 217437.30
!CHECK 217440.00 | 217443.00+ 000 000005 000000 | line 10 MMCPCW CW,MCPBAD,5.0 -WRITE CW -- the count field is a REAL check of MCPBAD landing at 217443.00 across the DRZ on line 11
!CHECK 217443.00 | 1777777777777777777777 | line 12 MCPBAD DD(BU),(16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF -11111......
!CHECK 217444.00 | 1252525252525252525252 | line 13 DD(BU),(16)AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA -........
!CHECK 217445.00 | 1777777777740000000000 | line 14 DD(BU),(16)FFFFFFFF00000000 -111111......
!CHECK 217446.00 | 176775 | line 15 DD(BU,16),(16)FDFD -TWO CARRIAGE RETURNS -- 16 bits, so the entry-mode DD on line 16 starts at the printed 217446.20 | 16
!CHECK 217451.00 | 000000.00+ | line 18 ZEC75S VF,0.0
!CHECK 217451.40 | 000000.00+ | line 19 SDISIC VF,0 -LOCATION GENERATING ERROR CODE -- the defining card for the symbol pp.103/119/120/124/129/130 back-derived
!CHECK 217452.00 | 217452.52 C6 | line 21 SDSPDS BIFZ,$.32 -- .32 written decimal, printed 0o40 plus BIFZ's 0o12; this address is p.103 line 43's SDISIC+.32
!CHECK 217452.40 | 000040.35 01 | line 22 LVI,$14,32.0 -- 32 decimal words is 0o40
!CHECK 217453.00 | 215265.35 D0 | line 23 SVA,$14,STIC (same card as line 22)
!CHECK 217453.40 | 000003.00 80 215230.34 A0 | line 24 TI,14,3.0,STLR -- the second operand's offset is 2*14 = 0o34, which is what encodes the "14"
!CHECK 217454.40 | 000021.00 80 215246.36 A0 | line 25 TI,15,17.0,STLR+14.0 (same card as 24) -- 17 decimal is 0o21, STLR+14 words is 215246, offset 2*15 = 0o36
!CHECK 217455.40 | 215231.47 A0 | line 26 BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101 -- every mask bit, the .26 and the 2 are all visible in this half word; see GLYPHS (3)
